(kicad_sch
	(version 20260306)
	(generator "eeschema")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(uuid "b33e0d4a-cbbf-4030-9279-e2ab0e38b6f1")
	(paper "A4")
	(title_block
		(title "Notes")
		(date "2026-08-18")
		(rev "2.0")
		(company "JRSeti")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "Purpose: Control dual axes of a motor controlled\nsystem, hosted by an on-board Raspberry Pi CM4.\n\n- Modbus RTU commands from the on-board CM4 over\n  a 3.3V full-duplex UART (STM32 USART1)\n- MCU outputs motor PWM, direction, enable/disable\n- Input from encoder connected to motor output\n- Host provides configuration and position commands\n- MCU runs a PID loop to position/move motors\n- Onboard temperature sensor, MCU can turn fan on/off\n- I2C extender for sensors placed at the axes\n- Isolated RS485 leader port (USART3) for downstream\n  devices\n- NMEA sentences and 1PPS from a MAX-M10S GPS\n- CM4 carrier: gigabit Ethernet, 2x USB 2.0 behind a\n  USB2514B hub, micro-USB OTG for rpiboot"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.956 45.466 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "502df861-08d4-4a8e-b2dc-f427feabe0a0")
	)
	(text "MCU Specifications\nPart Number: STM32G474RET6\nPackage: LQFP64\nClock: 170 MHz (16 MHz HSE, PLL /4 x85 /2)\nFlash: 512 KB\nRAM: 128 KB\n\nSpeed and position commands are received from the\non-board CM4 over USART1 (3.3V, full duplex).\nModbus node address is fixed at 1 - the link is\npoint-to-point, so there is no bus to address.\nEncoder is the E6B2-CWZ6C.\nMotor Controller: DM556Y.\nProgram/debug: ST STDC14, SWD + SWO, STLINK-V3MINIE.\nI2C for reading I2C sensors.\n2 Limit switches."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.876 82.804 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5e94f6af-6242-483e-96b4-dd7da6174902")
	)
	(text "CM4 power-fail strategy: read-only root\nplus f2fs on the data partition, and no\nhold-up capacitor bank. It costs nothing,\nit is the approach deployed Pi products\nuse, and it removes the failure mode\ninstead of racing it.\n\nAdd power-fail detection later only if\nrecording data is actually being lost.\nThat is a software-observable problem,\nso it will be obvious."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.29 181.356 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5fbda5c0-4caa-4435-98ae-a9a89cc8c186")
	)
	(text "Changes for V2.0\n\n- Add Raspberry Pi CM4 carrier (2x DF40C-100DS-0.4V)\n- Gigabit Ethernet, 2x USB 2.0 via USB2514B hub\n- micro-USB OTG for rpiboot eMMC programming\n- Remove RS485 device port, USART1 now goes to the CM4\n- ADDR0-2 / CONFIG_SW repurposed as SW1-SW4\n- 12V to 5V buck (AP64501) for CM4 and both USB ports"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.194 155.194 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "93e6b977-318f-4557-be53-c601c1c70544")
	)
	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.798 20.828 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5.08 5.08)
			)
		)
		(uuid "bec4a1e9-2156-449d-a699-b91cfad0b06f")
	)
	(text "This STM32 can be clocked up to 170MHz and runs at that\nspeed. Reducing the clock was considered to weaken\nharmonics above 1GHz, but has not been implemented -\nevery firmware revision to date runs at 170MHz. If RFI\nis ever measured as a real problem, the rate can be\nlowered in SystemClock_Config."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.876 113.792 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "dda6f144-5632-48c0-a16a-8884b502e30c")
	)
